Relevant columns, their potential usage, and likely conditions  
• races.year – filter to seasons 2001 and later (WHERE year >= 2001).  
• races.round – locate the last (max) round in each year to know the “final‑race” race_id that contains the season‑ending points table.  
• races.race_id – join key to driver_standings and results.  
• driver_standings.race_id – pick only the standings of the final race of every season.  
• driver_standings.driver_id – identifies each driver; also used to join to results/drivers tables.  
• driver_standings.points – season‑total points for the driver at that moment; keep rows WHERE points > 0 (i.e., “point‑scoring drivers”) and later find the MIN() per season.  
• results.driver_id / results.race_id / results.constructor_id – lets us find which constructor the “lowest‑scoring” driver was driving for at the last race of that season.  
• constructors.constructor_id / constructors.name – convert constructor_id to human‑readable constructor name.  
• drivers.driver_id / drivers.forename / drivers.surname – optional for inspection.

Ten exploratory SQLite queries (each different, each limited to 20 rows)  
```sql
-- 1. View races (year, round, race_id) from 2001 onward
SELECT year, round, race_id
FROM races
WHERE year >= 2001
ORDER BY year ASC, round DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- 2. For every season ≥2001, show the highest round number (= last GP of season)
SELECT year, MAX(round) AS final_round
FROM races
WHERE year >= 2001
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;

-- 3. Find the race_id of the final round of the 2001 season (example season)
SELECT race_id, name
FROM races
WHERE year = 2001
  AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
LIMIT 20;

-- 4. Show driver standings for that final 2001 race_id
SELECT ds.driver_id, ds.points, ds.position
FROM driver_standings AS ds
WHERE ds.race_id = (
      SELECT race_id FROM races
      WHERE year = 2001
        AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
)
ORDER BY ds.position
LIMIT 20;

-- 5. Filter only the point‑scoring drivers (>0) in that race_id
SELECT driver_id, points
FROM driver_standings
WHERE race_id = (
      SELECT race_id FROM races
      WHERE year = 2001
        AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
)
  AND points > 0
ORDER BY points
LIMIT 20;

-- 6. Get the minimum positive points and the driver(s) who had them in 2001
SELECT driver_id, points
FROM driver_standings
WHERE race_id = (
      SELECT race_id FROM races
      WHERE year = 2001
        AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
)
  AND points = (
      SELECT MIN(points) FROM driver_standings
      WHERE race_id = (
            SELECT race_id FROM races
            WHERE year = 2001
              AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
      )
        AND points > 0
)
LIMIT 20;

-- 7. Add driver names to that “fewest‑points” set
SELECT d.forename || ' ' || d.surname AS driver_name,
       ds.points
FROM driver_standings AS ds
JOIN drivers AS d ON d.driver_id = ds.driver_id
WHERE ds.race_id = (
      SELECT race_id FROM races
      WHERE year = 2001
        AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
)
  AND ds.points = (
      SELECT MIN(points) FROM driver_standings
      WHERE race_id = (
            SELECT race_id FROM races
            WHERE year = 2001
              AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
      )
        AND points > 0
)
LIMIT 20;

-- 8. Link those driver(s) to the constructor they drove for in that race
SELECT r.constructor_id,
       d.forename || ' ' || d.surname AS driver_name,
       ds.points
FROM driver_standings AS ds
JOIN results           AS r ON r.race_id   = ds.race_id
                           AND r.driver_id = ds.driver_id
JOIN drivers           AS d ON d.driver_id = ds.driver_id
WHERE ds.race_id = (
      SELECT race_id FROM races
      WHERE year = 2001
        AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
)
  AND ds.points = (
      SELECT MIN(points) FROM driver_standings
      WHERE race_id = (
            SELECT race_id FROM races
            WHERE year = 2001
              AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
      )
        AND points > 0
)
LIMIT 20;

-- 9. Add constructor names
SELECT c.name   AS constructor_name,
       d.forename || ' ' || d.surname AS driver_name,
       ds.points
FROM driver_standings AS ds
JOIN results           AS r ON r.race_id   = ds.race_id
                           AND r.driver_id = ds.driver_id
JOIN constructors      AS c ON c.constructor_id = r.constructor_id
JOIN drivers           AS d ON d.driver_id = ds.driver_id
WHERE ds.race_id = (
      SELECT race_id FROM races
      WHERE year = 2001
        AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
)
  AND ds.points = (
      SELECT MIN(points) FROM driver_standings
      WHERE race_id = (
            SELECT race_id FROM races
            WHERE year = 2001
              AND round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2001)
      )
        AND points > 0
)
LIMIT 20;

-- 10. One‑shot: across all seasons ≥2001, count how many times each constructor
-- supplied the driver(s) with the fewest positive points, then list top five
WITH final_races AS (
    SELECT year,
           MAX(round) AS final_round,
           MAX(race_id) AS final_race_id
    FROM races
    WHERE year >= 2001
    GROUP BY year
),
fewest_pts AS (
    SELECT fr.year,
           ds.driver_id,
           ds.points,
           r.constructor_id
    FROM final_races AS fr
    JOIN driver_standings AS ds ON ds.race_id = fr.final_race_id
    JOIN results          AS r  ON r.race_id  = ds.race_id
                                AND r.driver_id = ds.driver_id
    WHERE ds.points > 0
      AND ds.points = (
            SELECT MIN(points)
            FROM driver_standings
            WHERE race_id = fr.final_race_id
              AND points > 0
      )
)
SELECT c.name AS constructor_name,
       COUNT(*) AS seasons_as_lowest_points_constructor
FROM fewest_pts
JOIN constructors AS c ON c.constructor_id = fewest_pts.constructor_id
GROUP BY fewest_pts.constructor_id
ORDER BY seasons_as_lowest_points_constructor DESC, constructor_name
LIMIT 20;
```
